-- title:
--   Kummer theory for K(√[n]u : u ∈ S)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, let $n$ be a natural number, and assume that the set `primitiveRoots n K` of primitive $n$-th roots of unity in $K$ is nonempty. Let $S$ be a finite set of units of $K$, and assume that $L$ is a splitting field over $K$ of the polynomial $\prod_{u \in S}(X^{n} - u)$, the product being taken over $S$ with each unit $u$ regarded as an element of $K$. The conclusion identifies the subgroup [`groupCohomology.Kummer.powerSubgroup K L n`](def/GroupCohomology_Kummer.html#L157) of $K^\times$, consisting of those units $a$ for which there exists a unit $\alpha$ of $L$ with $\mathrm{algebraMap}_{K,L}(a) = \alpha^{n}$, with the join in the lattice of subgroups of $K^\times$ of the subgroup generated by $S$ and the image of the $n$-th power homomorphism `powMonoidHom n` on $K^\times$. In other words, a unit of $K$ becomes an $n$-th power in $L$ precisely when it is the product of an element of $\langle S \rangle$ and an $n$-th power in $K^\times$.
--
--   This is the standard Kummer-theoretic description of $K^\times \cap (L^\times)^{n}$ for the radical extension $L = K\bigl(u^{1/n} : u \in S\bigr)$ of a field containing a primitive $n$-th root of unity; the inclusion of the right-hand side is immediate, and the reverse inclusion is a counting argument comparing the order of $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ with the index $[\langle S\rangle (K^\times)^{n} : (K^\times)^{n}]$, using that a $K$-automorphism of $L$ fixing all chosen $n$-th roots is trivial. It is used in the construction of auxiliary abelian extensions of number fields, both in an idelic form and in the analysis of inertia at primes where a prescribed element becomes an $n$-th power.
-- source:
